  "name": "your stone pit",
  "note": "YOUR worked pit at home — you dug it on day 4 hunting furnace stone, and its floor is where the stone is. Bounds: columns (65..66, -92), floor at y63, a few blocks deep below the pad. THE WAY OUT IS YOUR OWN STAIR: the dirt stair you built against its west side, up to (64, 66, -92), and from there onto the pad. You ended day 4 standing at its floor beside that stair, one climb short. This pit is not a trap and not the pocket — it is a place you work: down the stair to dig stone, up the stair to get out.",
