 {
  "name": "the pocket that held me",
  "note": "The low pocket in the dip, south-east of home — this spot is its mouth, the lip you cross to drop in. Yesterday it held you for an hour while you hunted furnace stone, and when the spiders and the bow skeleton came, the old flee could not get you out: you died there four times and lost everything you carried. Your table still stands in its depths at (77, 64, -98). The ground in there is broken steps; the only ways out are short hops, up and over the lip. You may refuse this place. Stone exists elsewhere.",
